{"t": 1794104740.7996604, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change (commit 8c2f1d0) introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue: [LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit](https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/)\n\nReplacing Decimal rounding with `int(...)` truncates the converted amount instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so totals are off by 1 minor unit (e.g. expected 1100, got 1099). First seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3, ~2,201 events.\n\nFix in `worker/rates.py`: restore rounding via `Decimal(...).quantize(Decimal(\"1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` before converting to int.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
